1
00:00:03,145 --> 00:00:07,362
Rosa said my name. I almost shouted hers.

2
00:00:07,362 --> 00:00:10,210
The officer covered the radio speaker with his hand.

3
00:00:10,210 --> 00:00:13,957
Above us, something scraped along the pavement.

4
00:00:13,957 --> 00:00:18,125
A shoe dragged. Stopped. Dragged again.

5
00:00:18,125 --> 00:00:20,400
I held the button close to my mouth.

6
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:25,630
I'm here. For a moment, I heard nothing but her breathing.

7
00:00:25,630 --> 00:00:28,512
Then she said, stay below the road.

8
00:00:28,512 --> 00:00:34,134
I'll get you across. The canal separated us from a row of dark buildings.

9
00:00:34,134 --> 00:00:37,446
Somewhere among them, Rosa was sitting beside a microphone.

10
00:00:37,446 --> 00:00:42,352
I searched every window until the officer pulled me back beneath the concrete embankment.

11
00:00:42,352 --> 00:00:45,263
Finding her voice hadn't made the street any safer.

12
00:00:45,263 --> 00:00:48,624
The maintenance worker could barely put weight on his injured leg.

13
00:00:48,624 --> 00:00:53,236
The older woman had taken his bag, but every few steps we still had to

14
00:00:53,236 --> 00:00:56,561
stop. Rosa guided us toward a pumping station beneath the road.

15
00:00:56,561 --> 00:00:58,439
Its upper office was empty.

16
00:00:58,439 --> 00:01:01,773
The inspection steps outside disappeared into black water.

17
00:01:01,773 --> 00:01:04,119
The lower crossing was flooded.

18
00:01:04,119 --> 00:01:06,466
We couldn't reach her yet.

19
00:01:06,466 --> 00:01:10,965
By the time we secured the office door, the light outside had faded.

20
00:01:10,965 --> 00:01:16,545
We spent our second night sitting against the walls, sharing the water we had left.

21
00:01:16,545 --> 00:01:18,866
The worker slept in short bursts.

22
00:01:18,866 --> 00:01:20,626
The officer watched the door.

23
00:01:20,626 --> 00:01:23,670
I kept the radio against my chest.

24
00:01:23,670 --> 00:01:27,007
Whenever the static changed, I woke.

25
00:01:27,007 --> 00:01:30,064
Just before dawn, Rosa came back.

26
00:01:30,064 --> 00:01:32,870
Look across the canal. Second floor.

27
00:01:32,870 --> 00:01:37,137
The narrow window. A flashlight blinked behind the glass.

28
00:01:37,137 --> 00:01:42,247
I raised my hand. The light moved from side to side.

29
00:01:42,247 --> 00:01:46,111
Other hand, she said. I switched.

30
00:01:46,111 --> 00:01:50,586
She laughed once, quietly, and then stopped herself.

31
00:01:50,586 --> 00:01:54,732
I hadn't realized how badly I needed to hear a sound like that.

32
00:01:54,732 --> 00:01:57,572
The third morning arrived without sunlight.

33
00:01:57,572 --> 00:02:01,917
Smoke covered the rooftops, turning the canal the color of dirty metal.

34
00:02:01,917 --> 00:02:05,640
In the pale light, we could finally see the main bridge.

35
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:08,170
A bus stood across its entrance.

36
00:02:08,170 --> 00:02:11,596
Beyond it, part of the roadway had collapsed.

37
00:02:11,596 --> 00:02:15,046
People moved between the abandoned vehicles, but from that distance I couldn't tell

38
00:02:15,046 --> 00:02:19,395
who was searching for a way through and who was simply following the noise.

39
00:02:19,395 --> 00:02:22,037
Rosa told us to stop looking at it.

40
00:02:22,037 --> 00:02:24,023
There are maintenance steps below you.

41
00:02:24,023 --> 00:02:26,497
They lead to a walkway across the lock.

42
00:02:26,497 --> 00:02:29,837
I can lower the water enough to expose it.

43
00:02:29,837 --> 00:02:33,867
The worker pulled himself toward a diagram bolted to the office wall.

44
00:02:33,867 --> 00:02:36,600
He wiped the dirt from its glass.

45
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:40,398
For the first time all night, he had something useful to study.

46
00:02:40,398 --> 00:02:44,745
While he traced the pipework, the officer sat beside me.

47
00:02:44,745 --> 00:02:46,969
Your arm. I looked down.

48
00:02:46,969 --> 00:02:50,056
A dark patch had spread through the bandage.

49
00:02:50,056 --> 00:02:52,757
He had seen it at the school.

50
00:02:52,757 --> 00:02:55,606
He had helped me climb the stairs without asking.

51
00:02:55,606 --> 00:02:59,391
Now there was nowhere left for the question to wait.

52
00:02:59,391 --> 00:03:04,003
What happened? I don't know what it means.

53
00:03:04,003 --> 00:03:06,401
That wasn't what I asked.

54
00:03:06,401 --> 00:03:09,901
I loosened the cloth enough to show him.

55
00:03:09,901 --> 00:03:14,049
He looked carefully, then handed the bandage back.

56
00:03:14,049 --> 00:03:18,406
We tell them before we go inside.

57
00:03:18,406 --> 00:03:22,064
I nodded. He stayed beside me.

58
00:03:22,064 --> 00:03:25,813
Across the canal, Rosa opened the downstream gate.

59
00:03:25,813 --> 00:03:28,559
At first, nothing seemed to happen.

60
00:03:28,559 --> 00:03:31,946
Then a pale line appeared against the nearest inspection step.

61
00:03:31,946 --> 00:03:35,778
Water slid away from the concrete.

62
00:03:35,778 --> 00:03:38,764
Another step emerged beneath it.

63
00:03:38,764 --> 00:03:43,021
Farther along the bank, the discharge outlet began to roar.

64
00:03:43,021 --> 00:03:45,727
Shapes moved on the road above us.

65
00:03:45,727 --> 00:03:48,776
The infected were turning toward the sound.

66
00:03:48,776 --> 00:03:51,960
The worker pointed through the office window.

67
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:55,472
The outlet's west. We cross east.

68
00:03:55,472 --> 00:03:58,376
For once, the noise was opening a path.

69
00:03:58,376 --> 00:04:04,561
We prepared without speaking. The older woman tore a strip from the lining of her

70
00:04:04,561 --> 00:04:06,413
bag and wrapped the worker's keys.

71
00:04:06,413 --> 00:04:12,266
I remembered him opening the school door, how enormous that little turn of metal had

72
00:04:12,266 --> 00:04:15,213
sounded. The officer checked the steps.

73
00:04:15,213 --> 00:04:18,300
I secured the radio inside my coat.

74
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:21,466
Then the worker took the older woman's hand.

75
00:04:21,466 --> 00:04:24,174
If I stop, keep going.

76
00:04:24,174 --> 00:04:26,350
She tightened the cloth around his keys.

77
00:04:26,350 --> 00:04:30,026
You can tell me that on the other side.

78
00:04:30,026 --> 00:04:33,550
The first section of walkway emerged from the water.

79
00:04:33,550 --> 00:04:36,353
It was narrower than I had expected.

80
00:04:36,353 --> 00:04:39,213
A low rail ran along one edge.

81
00:04:39,213 --> 00:04:42,274
The other dropped straight into the canal.

82
00:04:42,274 --> 00:04:44,001
Mud covered the metal plates.

83
00:04:44,001 --> 00:04:47,404
The officer went first, testing each foothold.

84
00:04:47,404 --> 00:04:51,414
The older woman followed, keeping one hand on his shoulder.

85
00:04:51,414 --> 00:04:53,726
Halfway across, she looked back.

86
00:04:53,726 --> 00:04:57,900
I raised my hand. This time, it was a promise.

87
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:00,073
The worker and I started down.

88
00:05:00,073 --> 00:05:02,925
His injured leg shook on the final step.

89
00:05:02,925 --> 00:05:07,046
I took his weight before his boot reached the walkway, and together we moved beyond

90
00:05:07,046 --> 00:05:12,230
the pumping station. Behind us, the access gate swung against its frame.

91
00:05:12,230 --> 00:05:15,340
A thin metallic squeal rose above the water.

92
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:18,677
On the road, one of the figures stopped.

93
00:05:18,677 --> 00:05:21,970
Its head turned. I pushed the worker forward.

94
00:05:21,970 --> 00:05:25,368
Don't look back. He looked anyway.

95
00:05:25,368 --> 00:05:30,112
The infected came down the upper steps slowly at first, following the rail with one

96
00:05:30,112 --> 00:05:33,150
hand. Then its foot struck the gate.

97
00:05:33,150 --> 00:05:37,001
The whole frame rattled. Two more shapes appeared behind it.

98
00:05:37,001 --> 00:05:41,050
I shoved the worker onto the first stretch of walkway and pulled the gate shut.

99
00:05:41,050 --> 00:05:45,686
The latch wouldn't catch. Something had bent the bracket away from the frame.

100
00:05:45,686 --> 00:05:47,800
A hand pushed through the gap.

101
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:50,255
I drove my shoulder against the metal.

102
00:05:50,255 --> 00:05:51,900
Pain tore through my arm.

103
00:05:51,900 --> 00:05:53,919
The worker turned to come back.

104
00:05:53,919 --> 00:05:58,507
Go, I said. He stayed where he was, staring past me.

105
00:05:58,507 --> 00:06:01,688
Then he pointed. A loose chain hung beneath the railing.

106
00:06:01,688 --> 00:06:04,866
I reached for it without taking my shoulder off the gate.

107
00:06:04,866 --> 00:06:06,681
My fingers closed around wet metal.

108
00:06:06,681 --> 00:06:11,365
I dragged the chain through the gate handle and around the nearest post.

109
00:06:11,365 --> 00:06:14,564
The first loop slipped. The second held.

110
00:06:14,564 --> 00:06:17,992
By then, the officer was coming back along the walkway.

111
00:06:17,992 --> 00:06:20,570
I wanted to tell him to stay with the others.

112
00:06:20,570 --> 00:06:23,163
Instead, I took his hand.

113
00:06:23,163 --> 00:06:26,341
We crossed together. The chain snapped tight behind us.

114
00:06:26,341 --> 00:06:30,874
A metal plate shifted beneath my boot, and for a second I saw the water

115
00:06:30,874 --> 00:06:33,338
between my feet. The officer caught my coat.

116
00:06:33,338 --> 00:06:36,797
On the far bank, the older woman and Rosa were helping the worker through an

117
00:06:36,797 --> 00:06:41,120
open service entrance. Rosa. No glass between us now.

118
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:44,970
No static. She held the door while we climbed the last steps.

119
00:06:44,970 --> 00:06:49,189
The officer pulled it shut, and Rosa dropped a steel bar into its brackets.

120
00:06:49,189 --> 00:06:53,956
For a few seconds, all five of us stood in the little entrance chamber, listening.

121
00:06:53,956 --> 00:06:56,317
Then she put her arms around me.

122
00:06:56,317 --> 00:06:59,597
I had imagined asking her a hundred questions.

123
00:06:59,597 --> 00:07:02,353
I couldn't remember any of them.

124
00:07:02,353 --> 00:07:05,123
There was a small shelter beyond the chamber.

125
00:07:05,123 --> 00:07:07,560
Mattresses lined a dry corridor.

126
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:09,625
Water containers stood beneath a table.

127
00:07:09,625 --> 00:07:15,440
A receiver, two lamps and a battery meter occupied the room behind the narrow window.

128
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:18,870
Someone had marked the drinking water in careful pencil lines.

129
00:07:18,870 --> 00:07:22,454
The place smelled of damp clothes and boiled food.

130
00:07:22,454 --> 00:07:25,631
I had spent two days looking for somewhere safe.

131
00:07:25,631 --> 00:07:29,831
Standing there, I realized how little I needed it to look like safety.

132
00:07:29,831 --> 00:07:33,711
Before Rosa could lead me farther inside, I showed her the bandage.

133
00:07:33,711 --> 00:07:36,723
The officer stood beside me while I explained.

134
00:07:36,723 --> 00:07:41,506
She listened without interrupting. Then she brought clean cloth and a basin.

135
00:07:41,506 --> 00:07:43,417
She didn't tell me it was nothing.

136
00:07:43,417 --> 00:07:45,734
She didn't tell me I would be fine.

137
00:07:45,734 --> 00:07:48,851
We agreed I would stay in the entrance room, where they could watch me and

138
00:07:48,851 --> 00:07:51,925
I could keep some distance from the others.

139
00:07:51,925 --> 00:07:56,337
The door remained open. Across the corridor, the worker finally lay down.

140
00:07:56,337 --> 00:08:01,086
The older woman sat beside him with his wrapped keys in her lap.

141
00:08:01,086 --> 00:08:03,565
Later, I told Rosa about the school.

142
00:08:03,565 --> 00:08:05,711
The passage beneath the gym.

143
00:08:05,711 --> 00:08:09,575
The door marked seventeen. The warning we had restored.

144
00:08:09,575 --> 00:08:13,261
When I mentioned the signature, she looked toward the receiver.

145
00:08:13,261 --> 00:08:15,087
I helped test that relay.

146
00:08:15,087 --> 00:08:17,510
Four days before? She nodded.

147
00:08:17,510 --> 00:08:21,698
Before any of this? Before anyone told us what was happening.

148
00:08:21,698 --> 00:08:24,173
She opened a folder beneath the desk.

149
00:08:24,173 --> 00:08:26,618
The first sheet was an equipment checklist.

150
00:08:26,618 --> 00:08:29,179
The second was a handwritten call log.

151
00:08:29,179 --> 00:08:31,554
Several lines had been crossed out.

152
00:08:31,554 --> 00:08:36,291
Beside one entry, someone had written a different address and underlined it twice.

153
00:08:36,291 --> 00:08:39,554
Rosa placed her finger beneath the original note.

154
00:08:39,554 --> 00:08:43,730
Ambulance crew requesting assistance. Violent patient.

155
00:08:43,730 --> 00:08:47,275
Additional injuries. The date matched the transmission test.

156
00:08:47,275 --> 00:08:51,920
Four days earlier. That could have been anything, I said.

157
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:54,600
It could. She turned the page.

158
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:58,697
Another call. Another crew. The same building.

159
00:08:58,697 --> 00:09:05,970
The west hospital annex. Rosa had written down the requests because that was her job

160
00:09:05,970 --> 00:09:08,875
at the relay: listen, record, pass them on.

161
00:09:08,875 --> 00:09:13,298
She had never received an answer she could send back.

162
00:09:13,298 --> 00:09:17,893
Before I could ask another question, a clear voice came through the receiver.

163
00:09:17,893 --> 00:09:21,718
Municipal emergency service. Main bridge access is open.

164
00:09:21,718 --> 00:09:24,670
Proceed to the designated evacuation point.

165
00:09:24,670 --> 00:09:29,561
The officer stood up. Outside, beyond the narrow window, people were moving toward

166
00:09:29,561 --> 00:09:32,370
the bridge. The announcement repeated.

167
00:09:32,370 --> 00:09:35,884
Exactly the same words. Exactly the same pause.

168
00:09:35,884 --> 00:09:39,804
I heard that at the evacuation barrier, the officer said.

169
00:09:39,804 --> 00:09:43,602
We watched a man lift a child over the bumper of an abandoned car.

170
00:09:43,602 --> 00:09:46,316
Behind them, more people turned toward the bridge.

171
00:09:46,316 --> 00:09:48,141
It might have been an old recording.

172
00:09:48,141 --> 00:09:50,797
It might have been a terrible mistake.

173
00:09:50,797 --> 00:09:52,838
Either way, they were following it.

174
00:09:52,838 --> 00:09:54,873
Rosa reached for the transmitter.

175
00:09:54,873 --> 00:09:57,146
The officer looked toward the entrance chamber.

176
00:09:57,146 --> 00:10:00,661
Beyond our door, the infected were still somewhere along the canal.

177
00:10:00,661 --> 00:10:04,477
If they hear this station— I know, she said.

178
00:10:04,477 --> 00:10:06,442
Her hand remained above the switch.

179
00:10:06,442 --> 00:10:09,126
All night, her voice had given us somewhere to go.

180
00:10:09,126 --> 00:10:12,592
Now people outside were being led toward a broken road.

181
00:10:12,592 --> 00:10:16,268
I pulled a chair beside the desk and sat down before my legs could give

182
00:10:16,268 --> 00:10:18,092
way. Tell them what we saw.

183
00:10:18,092 --> 00:10:21,430
Rosa pressed the button. This is the canal relay.

184
00:10:21,430 --> 00:10:23,027
The main bridge is damaged.

185
00:10:23,027 --> 00:10:25,027
Do not approach the central span.

186
00:10:25,027 --> 00:10:28,303
Repeat, the evacuation announcement is incorrect.

187
00:10:28,303 --> 00:10:31,057
She released it. We waited.

188
00:10:31,057 --> 00:10:34,602
Across the canal, the man carrying the child stopped beside a car.

189
00:10:34,602 --> 00:10:37,362
Someone behind him pointed away from the bridge.

190
00:10:37,362 --> 00:10:39,110
Rosa began the warning again.

191
00:10:39,110 --> 00:10:41,635
A second voice cut across hers.

192
00:10:41,635 --> 00:10:46,087
Canal station. Stop transmitting. Her finger lifted from the button.

193
00:10:46,087 --> 00:10:49,706
The officer moved closer. The voice returned.

194
00:10:49,706 --> 00:10:52,038
Leave the evacuation message alone.

195
00:10:52,038 --> 00:10:54,074
Rosa checked the receiver settings.

196
00:10:54,074 --> 00:10:55,298
Then she checked them again.

197
00:10:55,298 --> 00:10:57,461
What is it? I asked.

198
00:10:57,461 --> 00:10:59,054
She turned the call log toward me.

199
00:10:59,054 --> 00:11:01,934
Beside the requests from the hospital was a channel number.

200
00:11:01,934 --> 00:11:05,067
The one now showing on the receiver.

201
00:11:05,067 --> 00:11:07,765
The instructions came through here, she said.

202
00:11:07,765 --> 00:11:09,964
They told us to keep recording the calls.

203
00:11:09,964 --> 00:11:12,458
Who did? She looked at the microphone.

204
00:11:12,458 --> 00:11:14,790
I never got a name.

205
00:11:14,790 --> 00:11:17,610
Outside, the announcement began again.

206
00:11:17,610 --> 00:11:20,087
Main bridge access is open.

207
00:11:20,087 --> 00:11:22,090
Rosa took a breath and reached for the switch.

208
00:11:22,090 --> 00:11:25,141
This time, none of us tried to stop her.

209
00:11:25,141 --> 00:11:27,481
Somewhere in the city, someone had heard our warning.

210
00:11:27,481 --> 00:11:29,160
And they wanted us quiet.
